From 9dbcb55a8a4bcd6eb8b807142d95087fae6be117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blue Cuenca <blue.cuenca@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 16:32:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 66/69] aic_load_fw: fix FORTIFY_SOURCE false positive in
 aicbt_patch_info_unpack
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The memcpy destination was &patch_info->adid_addrinf (a single uint32_t,
4 bytes), but the copy size was info_len*8 bytes. FORTIFY_SOURCE fires a
WARNING because it sees destination object size = 4 < copy size.

This is a false positive: the intent is to populate all struct fields
starting at adid_addrinf sequentially from firmware data, and the struct
has enough space (8 fields × 4 bytes = 32 bytes).

Fix by computing the destination as a runtime uint8_t* offset so
FORTIFY_SOURCE resolves the object size to the full struct rather than
the single field. Add an explicit bounds check and cap to protect against
genuinely oversized firmware data.

Signed-off-by: Blue Cuenca <blue.cuenca@gmail.com>
---
 .../wireless/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth.c   | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth.c
index 184d85711..0fc19fd71 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicbluetooth.c
@@ -1227,7 +1227,20 @@ int aicbt_patch_info_unpack(struct aicbt_patch_info_t *patch_info, struct aicbt_
         patch_info->info_len = head_t->len;
         if(patch_info->info_len == 0)
             return 0;
-        memcpy(&patch_info->adid_addrinf, head_t->data, patch_info->info_len * sizeof(uint32_t) * 2);
+        /* head_t->data contains info_len (addr, val) uint32_t pairs that map
+         * sequentially onto the struct fields starting at adid_addrinf.
+         * Use a runtime-computed pointer so FORTIFY_SOURCE uses the whole
+         * struct size rather than the single adid_addrinf field size. */
+        {
+            size_t copy_size = patch_info->info_len * sizeof(uint32_t) * 2;
+            size_t max_size = sizeof(*patch_info) -
+                              offsetof(struct aicbt_patch_info_t, adid_addrinf);
+            uint8_t *dst = (uint8_t *)patch_info +
+                           offsetof(struct aicbt_patch_info_t, adid_addrinf);
+            if (WARN_ON(copy_size > max_size))
+                copy_size = max_size;
+            memcpy(dst, head_t->data, copy_size);
+        }
     }
     return 0;
 }
